2
00:02:29,423 --> 00:02:32,423
ある国に ロバの娘がいました
In a certain country, there was a donkey's daughter.

3
00:02:33,233 --> 00:02:38,733
周りから見た彼女は それはそれは恵まれて見えました
To those around her, she seemed so very blessed.

4
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:44,693
ですが 彼女の心は 決して豊かではありません
But her heart was not rich at all.

5
00:02:45,333 --> 00:02:51,933
決められた人形のような生活 本当の私はなんだろう
Living like a prescribed doll, I wonder what the real me is.

6
00:02:54,553 --> 00:02:58,253
大きな大きな犬がいました
There was a big, big dog.

7
00:02:58,853 --> 00:03:04,353
周りを見渡すと みんな小さく愛される犬ばかり
Looking around, everyone was just small, beloved dogs.

8
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:09,593
自分だけ大きな姿に大きなど声
Only she had a large form and a loud voice.

9
00:03:10,153 --> 00:03:14,253
怖がらないで一緒に遊ぼうよ
Don't be scared, let's play together.

10
00:03:15,893 --> 00:03:19,393
とてもかっこつけがりの猫がいました
There was a very pretentious cat.

11
00:03:19,893 --> 00:03:24,393
みんなからは嘘つき呼ばわりされています
Everyone calls her a liar.

12
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:28,433
本当はみんなを楽しませたいだけなのに
Even though she just wants to make everyone happy,

13
00:03:28,933 --> 00:03:33,433
おもしろそうなことが大好きなだけさ
she just loves things that seem fun.

14
00:03:35,793 --> 00:03:39,493
毎日仕事があってうらやましいでしょう
You must be envious of having work every day,

15
00:03:40,093 --> 00:03:44,493
楽しくて愉快な農場さ
a fun and cheerful farm.

16
00:03:45,793 --> 00:03:49,493
だけど毎日同じことの繰り返し
But it's the repetition of the same thing every day.

17
00:03:50,793 --> 00:03:57,193
もっと私が輝ける場所があるんじゃないか
Isn't there a place where I can shine brighter?

18
00:03:58,793 --> 00:04:02,593
天下の大泥棒 金銀財宝に目がありません
A world-class thief with no eyes for gold or silver.

19
00:04:04,393 --> 00:04:07,793
でも悪いことはしたいんじゃない
But it's not that I want to do bad things.

20
00:04:08,493 --> 00:04:12,793
貧しいみんなを笑顔にしたいだけなのに
I just want to make the poor people smile,

21
00:04:13,193 --> 00:04:18,193
自分も笑顔になれたらどれだけいいのかな
how wonderful it would be if I could smile too.

22
00:04:21,893 --> 00:04:24,493
大きな悩みを抱えたロバたち
Donkeys carrying big worries,

23
00:04:25,493 --> 00:04:31,993
君たちの物語が今 ここから始まっていくのです
your story is now beginning from here.

24
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:49,100
音楽 それは私たちの人生に彩りを 勇気を
Music, it brings color and courage to our lives,

25
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:54,000
そして夢を与えてくれる不思議な魔法
and a mysterious magic that gives us dreams.

26
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:59,000
これはそんな音楽の力を信じた動物たちの
This is the story of animals who believed in the power of music...

27
00:05:24,475 --> 00:05:27,575
ねえ 考えてもいいよ
Hey, you don't even have to think about it.

28
00:05:27,575 --> 00:05:30,875
口先じゃ分かり合えないの
We can't understand each other just with words.

29
00:05:30,875 --> 00:05:34,008
この音には今は乗ろうよ
Let's ride this sound right now.

30
00:05:34,008 --> 00:05:40,675
忘れないでいたいよ
I want to keep remembering it.

31
00:05:37,275 --> 00:05:40,675
身体は無彩色レイドバック
Our bodies are monochrome laid-back,

32
00:05:40,675 --> 00:05:43,775
ただうねる雨音でグルーヴ
grooving simply to the sound of rolling rain.

33
00:05:43,775 --> 00:05:47,375
ずっと二人で暮らそうよ この夜の隅っこで
Let's live together forever in the corner of this night.

34
00:05:47,375 --> 00:05:50,975
ねえ 不甲斐ない僕らに 誘ったのは君じゃないの
Hey, wasn't it you who invited us, us good-for-nothings?

35
00:05:50,975 --> 00:05:54,575
理屈だけじゃつまらないわ まだ時間が惜しいの
Logic alone is boring, and I still begrudge the time.

36
00:05:54,575 --> 00:05:58,175
練り歩く景色を真空パック 踏み鳴らす足音でグルーヴ
Vacuum-packing the strolling scenery, grooving to the stamping footsteps.

37
00:05:58,175 --> 00:06:03,008
まるで僕らはブレーメン たった二人だけのマーチ
We're just like Bremen, a march of just the two of us.

38
00:06:04,775 --> 00:06:08,075
決められたタスク 決められた笑顔で
With prescribed tasks and a prescribed smile,

39
00:06:08,075 --> 00:06:11,475
決められた人生を歩くの
walking down a prescribed life.

40
00:06:11,475 --> 00:06:14,975
何が私で何が私じゃないか
What is me, and what is not me?

41
00:06:14,975 --> 00:06:18,475
さっぱりわからない
I have no idea at all.

42
00:06:18,475 --> 00:06:21,875
手の物を捨てて 歌を歌えば
If I throw away what's in my hands and sing a song,

43
00:06:26,175 --> 00:06:32,175
私は 本当の私になる
I will become my true self.

44
00:06:32,875 --> 00:06:36,475
虹の入り江 森のカリブー
The rainbow inlet, the forest caribou—

45
00:06:36,475 --> 00:06:40,275
どこでもゆける 何にでもなれる
I can go anywhere, I can become anything,

46
00:06:40,275 --> 00:06:49,875
歌の世界なら
if it's in the world of song.

47
00:06:50,808 --> 00:06:56,008
石油の国の皆様、この度はブレーメンミュージックフェスを開催致します！
Everyone in the oil kingdom, welcome to the Bremen Music Festival!

48
00:06:56,008 --> 00:07:05,008
様々な世界の様々な物語が集まる歌の祭典。これよ、あなただけのお気に入りの音楽を見つけてください！
A festival of songs gathering various stories from various worlds. Find your favorite music here!

49
00:07:05,008 --> 00:07:07,808
私、決めたわ。
I've decided.

50
00:07:09,175 --> 00:07:13,675
ブレーメンへ行こう 本当の自分を見つけよう
Let's go to Bremen and find our true selves.

51
00:07:13,675 --> 00:07:19,275
世界を変える私だけの 歌を探して
Searching for the song that is uniquely mine to change the world.

52
00:07:22,008 --> 00:07:30,008
歌を探して
Searching for the song.

53
00:07:57,108 --> 00:08:03,208
ところで ブレーメンって どっちに行けばいいの？ こっち？ あっち？
By the way, which way should we go to Bremen? This way? That way?

54
00:08:04,108 --> 00:08:05,308
ワン！チャッ！
Woof! Cha!

55
00:08:06,608 --> 00:08:08,508
あー また驚かせちゃった
Ah, I surprised you again.

56
00:08:09,008 --> 00:08:15,208
本当は遊びたかっただけ
I really just wanted to play.

57
00:08:29,508 --> 00:08:33,508
チョービリー 声が大きくて
Cho-Billy, with such a loud voice,

58
00:08:35,508 --> 00:08:41,208
チョービリー 時間が強くて
Cho-Billy, with such strong time,

59
00:08:41,808 --> 00:08:51,008
周りと違うだけで 誰かを困らせてばかりの だめなやつさ
just being different, always troubling someone—such a useless fellow.

60
00:08:51,308 --> 00:08:55,008
あなた とっても素敵な声を持っているのに
You have such a wonderful voice, yet...

61
00:08:55,008 --> 00:08:58,208
そうかな 声が大きすぎて みんなを驚かせちゃうんだ
Is that so? My voice is too big and always surprises everyone.

62
00:08:58,208 --> 00:09:00,508
もう一度 聞かせてみて
Let me hear it one more time.

63
00:09:00,508 --> 00:09:04,508
それじゃ今度は 音楽に合わせて
Then this time, let's match it with the music!

64
00:09:05,008 --> 00:09:06,508
いいかい？吠えて！
Ready? Howl!

65
00:09:06,508 --> 00:09:07,508
ワン！
Woof!

66
00:09:07,508 --> 00:09:09,208
２回吠えて！
Howl twice!

67
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:10,508
ワン！ワン！
Woof! Woof!

68
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:14,008
ほら すべて綺麗でしょ
Look, isn't everything beautiful?

69
00:09:14,008 --> 00:09:20,008
重なれば どんなメロディだって
When they overlap, no matter what melody,

70
00:09:20,008 --> 00:09:26,508
居場所を見つけて 響き始める ミュージック
music starts to resonate, finding its place.

71
00:09:44,008 --> 00:09:50,008
ブレーメンへ行こう この声使えばできること
Let's go to Bremen! Whatever we can do using this voice,

72
00:09:50,508 --> 00:09:56,508
きっとあるはずだから 行こう 一緒に
I'm sure it's out there, so let's go together!

73
00:10:20,525 --> 00:10:22,475
さあ寄っていらっしゃい 見ていらっしゃい
Come on in and take a look!

74
00:10:22,805 --> 00:10:26,495
これより語るは甚だしき勇者の危機一髪な冒険譚
Now, I shall tell the tale of a hero's outrageous near-death adventure.

75
00:10:30,411 --> 00:10:32,501
家まで送ってもらいたいのに
Even though I want you to walk me home,

76
00:10:32,741 --> 00:10:34,921
今夜満たされたいのよ
I want to be fulfilled tonight.

77
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:37,401
できれば君にちょっと濡らして欲しいのよ
If possible, I want you to get me a little wet.

78
00:10:37,661 --> 00:10:39,481
酔いで寄りたいのよ
I want to get drunk and snuggle close,

79
00:10:39,711 --> 00:10:41,581
ごまかしてキスしたいのよ
Play it off and kiss you.

80
00:10:41,891 --> 00:10:43,741
君といたいよ 暗くてぬるい部屋で
I want to be with you in a dark, lukewarm room.

81
00:10:44,221 --> 00:10:45,381
なんかすごそう
"Sounds amazing"—

82
00:10:45,381 --> 00:10:50,571
ってどういう意味？ 朝まで待たせてお年寄りに説教を譲ったってこと？
What does that mean? That you made them wait till morning and left the scolding to an elderly person?

83
00:10:51,125 --> 00:10:55,695
さあ 艶やかな勇者に 勝算を
Now, what are the odds for this glamorous hero?

84
00:10:56,145 --> 00:10:58,355
奏でよう
Let's play!

85
00:10:59,625 --> 00:11:03,025
でも 決まって
But surely...

86
00:11:04,165 --> 00:11:08,595
ほら吹き回り 現実越えたクソ雑魚が
Look at this loudmouth, pathetic weakling surpassing reality—

87
00:11:08,995 --> 00:11:11,615
突き通せた
Piercing through it!

88
00:11:11,775 --> 00:11:15,135
美しいのに つまりそれって
Even though it's beautiful, meaning that—

89
00:11:16,055 --> 00:11:19,515
ともに奏でよ まだ見ぬゲスどものメロディを
Let's play together the melodies of unseen scumbags.

90
00:11:19,925 --> 00:11:24,105
はるか異国の地 開かれる歌劇
In a faraway foreign land, the opera opens.

91
00:11:24,245 --> 00:11:29,855
歌うというのか 面白い新たな冒険が
You say you'll sing? A fun, new adventure—

92
00:11:31,045 --> 00:11:36,485
よろしいわ 勝ち気らをささげよ
Very well, offer up your spirited selves!

93
00:11:37,035 --> 00:11:40,425
ブレメーへ行こう 嘘がもっと輝ける
Let's go to Bremen, where lies can shine even brighter.

94
00:11:40,685 --> 00:11:45,045
それが音楽だから行こう 一緒に
That's what music is, so let's go together!

95
00:11:52,945 --> 00:11:55,255
ブレメーへ行こう 嘘がもっと
Let's go to Bremen, where lies can shine—

96
00:11:55,625 --> 00:11:59,835
輝ける それが音楽だから行こう一緒に
Even brighter! That's what music is, so let's go together!

97
00:12:30,361 --> 00:12:37,081
一番いい役をやりましょう 誰よりも悲しくて殺せる役を
Let's play the best role, a role sadder and more fatal than anyone else's.

98
00:12:37,181 --> 00:12:44,221
四角い海の果てでも代わる代わるは人様演じている事それさえも忘れる世界
Even at the edge of the square sea, people take turns acting—a world where we forget even that we are acting.

99
00:12:44,401 --> 00:12:50,571
みんな籠の中の鳥 いつか抜け出す日夢見て やっと手にしたその時大空へと戸惑う mysterious
All birds in cages, dreaming of the day they'll break free. When they finally grasp it, they're bewildered towards the vast sky, mysterious.

100
00:12:50,931 --> 00:12:54,701
名前をあげて安心させましょう カットはかからない あなたの mysterious
Let's mention names to reassure. Cuts won't be called, your mysterious.

101
00:12:55,101 --> 00:13:00,021
星座を渡り紡ぎ 空へと逃げ仰せても 身体には懐かしさ 咽び捨てようもない ねぇねぇ
Even if we cross constellations and escape up to the sky, there's nostalgia in our bodies we can't choke down and throw away, hey, hey.

102
00:13:00,691 --> 00:13:06,031
時計のない国で 誰も要らないこの街で 熱い雪を降らす青い太陽
In a land without clocks, in a city where no one is needed, a blue sun rains down hot snow.

103
00:13:06,131 --> 00:13:10,301
窓もドアも壁もなく思い描く不死の鳥 間違いも答えもない自由へと彷徨う mysterious
With no windows, doors, or walls, the immortal bird we imagine wanders toward freedom with no mistakes or answers, mysterious.

104
00:13:10,891 --> 00:13:15,561
ひしめく羽を弾ませ 守るのは邪な清らかさ
Guarding the crowded feathers is a gentle purity,

105
00:13:15,561 --> 00:13:20,521
抱きしめられては飛び立つ 白紙に沈め墨たち 硬い水面泳ぐ髪
Embraced and taking flight. Sinking into blank paper, the ink stands out; hair swims on the solid water surface.

106
00:13:20,751 --> 00:13:25,811
通う息吹道連れに 諦めの帳ごふき 飛ぶ飛ば来い宵闇
With passing breaths as companions, wiping away the curtain of resignation, flying, flying, come, evening darkness.

107
00:13:25,891 --> 00:13:30,951
手折られた翼羽で 信じた呪いは願いは祈りは入れ墨 ひひとひらの仕草 mysterious
With severed wings, the curse we believed in, the wish, the prayer, a tattoo—a single gesture, mysterious.

108
00:13:40,771 --> 00:13:47,401
神や仏と悪魔のお友達 いてもいなくても私は mysterious あなたの mysterious
Friends with gods, buddhas, and demons; whether they're there or not, I'm mysterious, your mysterious.

109
00:13:48,351 --> 00:13:55,241
さあ一番いい役をやりましょう 星座渡り紡ぎ 空へと逃げ仰せても 身体には懐かしさ
Now, let's play the best role! Even if we cross constellations and escape up to the sky, there's nostalgia in our bodies—

110
00:13:55,421 --> 00:14:01,371
時計のない国で 誰も要らないこの街で 熱い雪を降らす青い太陽
In a land without clocks, in a city where no one is needed, a blue sun rains down hot snow.

111
00:14:01,421 --> 00:14:07,761
窓もドアも壁も風もなく 思い描く不死の鳥 間違いも答えもない 自由へと彷徨う mysterious
With no windows, doors, walls, or wind, the immortal bird we imagine wanders toward freedom with no mistakes or answers, mysterious.

112
00:14:26,521 --> 00:14:31,271
ひしめく羽を弾ませ 守るのは 邪な清らかさ 抱きしめられては飛び立つ
Guarding the crowded feathers is a gentle purity, embraced and taking flight.

113
00:14:31,271 --> 00:14:36,516
守るのは横島ぬしよだからさ 抱きしめられては飛び立つ
Protecting it is wickedness itself, embraced and taking flight.

114
00:14:51,016 --> 00:14:59,016
あふれしに沈め墨たち 硬いみなも泳ぐ髪 かよういる...
Sinking into overflowing ink, hair swimming on the solid water surface, passing breaths...

115
00:15:00,335 --> 00:15:01,835
今日は絶好調…そのはずでした過去形
Today's going great... or so I thought, past tense.

116
00:15:02,275 --> 00:15:05,015
天気予報ド外面 ドア閉まるバス 憂鬱なmonday
Weather forecast missed, bus door closing, gloomy Monday.

117
00:15:05,095 --> 00:15:06,965
なんて不条理文句 誰行き？hah…
Such absurd complaints, where is this headed? Hah...

118
00:15:06,965 --> 00:15:09,135
八つ当たりは問題外
Taking it out on others is out of the question.

119
00:15:09,305 --> 00:15:11,775
どうしようもないこと多すぎeveryday
Too many helpless things every single day,

120
00:15:11,995 --> 00:15:13,705
現実は手強い
Reality is tough.

121
00:15:13,935 --> 00:15:15,565
だけど試練の向こうへ
But beyond these trials,

122
00:15:15,705 --> 00:15:17,405
ため息ついてここから
Letting out a sigh, right from here

123
00:15:17,675 --> 00:15:19,355
立ち上がれたらまた
If we can stand back up, once again

124
00:15:19,515 --> 00:15:20,935
なにかが始まる
Something will begin.

125
00:15:21,055 --> 00:15:23,975
let's get it going now! going now!

126
00:15:24,445 --> 00:15:27,225
がむしゃら気味にどこへだって繰り出して
Recklessly venturing out anywhere,

127
00:15:27,375 --> 00:15:30,245
胸張って楽しんじゃおうup・down
Puffing out our chests to enjoy the ups and downs.

128
00:15:30,365 --> 00:15:33,475
say everyone, going now! going now!

129
00:15:33,745 --> 00:15:35,335
踊乱らしちゃえば
If we just shake things up,

130
00:15:35,555 --> 00:15:39,135
ああ、そうそう波乱万丈 大体の運命
Ah, yes, full of ups and downs, most of our fate

131
00:15:39,285 --> 00:15:41,895
変えてくのは自分だって――キミは知ってる
Is changed by ourselves—you already know that.

132
00:15:52,947 --> 00:15:55,697
一番いい役をやりにいこう
Let's go play the best role!

133
00:15:55,827 --> 00:16:00,524
やりましょう
Let's do it!

134
00:16:36,449 --> 00:16:38,229
頭でわかっては嘆いた
I understood it in my head and sighed,

135
00:16:38,229 --> 00:16:39,949
転がっていく様子を嘲った
Mocking how things kept tumbling down.

136
00:16:39,949 --> 00:16:42,529
